{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99568","id":2195935800,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6C41I4","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99568","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99568.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99568.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99568","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99568/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99568/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99568/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/c624e52c36a946949f12dd49c37f82a771541878","number":99568,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Make visual shader editor create node window a popup","user":{"login":"badsectoracula","id":20316467,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMzE2NDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20316467?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula","html_url":"https://github.com/badsectoracula","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/badsectoracula/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This makes the Visual Shader editor's \"Create Shader Node\" window to be a popup instead of a dialog, thus being easily dismissed by clicking outside the window like in most other DCC applications that use a node editor. It addresses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11213. It also solves the issue where the window would appear outside the screen area.\r\n\r\nPlease note that i have only tested this on Linux and X11.\r\n\r\n![add_node_popup](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fcd24652-91d8-44ad-bd6a-72fe97ccfff3)\r\n\r\nThe main negative with this patch is that unlike the window, the popup is not resizable and instead a 300px (scaled by `EDSCALE`) minimum width is used to ensure that the node names are visible. While it is possible to make the window resizable by setting the `Window::FLAG_RESIZE_DISABLED` to `false`, there is no visual indicator that the window is resizable and the window closes as soon as the resize finishes (seems a race condition between the window manager and the X11 mouse handling code for popups). Ideally there should be a control that can be placed on popups (like a small triangle at the bottom right corner, as that is common in various toolkits) to handle client-side resizing, but i can't find anything like that in Godot.\r\n\r\nA potential alternative would be to use the popup-based approach in this PR for right clicking but use a dialog when \"Add Node\" is selected from the popup menu. This will most likely require a larger change though as from what i can tell a window can't switch \"modes\" between being a Popup and a Dialog.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","descripti